<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103197" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέρσομαι</span></b> , 
			Pass.
		, with aor.
		inf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τερσῆναι, τερσήμεναι</span> (v. infr.), as if
		from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτέρσην</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be</i> or <i>become dry, dry
				up</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕλκος ἐτέρσετο παύσατο δ᾽
				αἷμα</span> the wound <i>dried up</i> and the blood was
			staunched, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.267
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				848
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέ μοι αἷμα τερσῆναι δύναται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					16.519
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θειλόπεδον τέρσεται ἠελίῳ</span>
			<i>is baked</i> by the sun, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				7.124
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἵματα δ᾽ ἠελίοιο μένον τερσήμεναι
					αὐγῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					6.98
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν [τὰ ῥάκεα] ἐν ἡλίῳ τέρσηται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Mul.</u>
					1.11
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσσε δακρυόφιν τέρσοντο</span>
			his eyes <i>became dry</i> from tears, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.152
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			 first in later 
				Ep.
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> using only <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τερσαίνω</span>),
				aor.
			subj.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέρσῃ </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-σει</span> codd.) <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				22.63
			</span></i>; inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέρσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					96
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				693
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέρσον</span>
			 both times); opt. 
				Med.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέρσαιο</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				709
			</span></i>:—<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> cites <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτέρρατο:
			ἐξηράνθη</span>. (Cf. Lat. <i>torreo, tostus</i>, Skt.
				<i>tŕṛ[snull ]yati</i> 'to be
			thirsty'.)</div>
